{"id":"dynamic_boat_wake","compound_name":"Graphs::Ocean::dynamic_boat_wake","source_path":"dynamic_boat_wake/dynamic_boat_wake.json","category":"Ocean","author":"Autodesk","description":"A procedural ocean surface with simulated wake and foam.","documentation_file":"dynamic_boat_wake_docs_ENU.md","documentation":"## Foamy Spectral Dynamic Ocean\n\n### What it does\n\nThis graph generates an procedural ocean surface with colliders.  Foam is generated on this surface.\n\n### Inputs and outputs\n\nThere are two mesh inputs.  One for the ocean surface (*mesh_plane*) and another for the collider object which generates the wake (*mesh_sphere*).  In the case of this graph, the collider mesh is output for visualization and the the ocean mesh is output with it's displacement and *foam* and *foam_color* properties.\n\n### How it works\n\n- The *source_dynamic_wave* compound generates the wake deformation.  That coupled with the *dynamic_wave_settings* is used to simulate the surface.  **Note:  ** This is a simulation, for best results, go back to the start of the timeline to reset the sim.\n\n- The *create_spectral_waves* compound generates a procedural ocean surface based on its settings.  This is **not ** a simulation, but a procedural surface. \n\n- Both of these then feed into the *simulate_foam* compound for the foam simulation.\n\n- The ocean surface mesh (*mesh_plane*) and the foam simulation are then plugged into the *wave_set_foam* compound, to set the *foam* attribute on the mesh plane.\n\n- The ocean surface mesh is fed into the *displace_by_wave* compound, along with both ocean displacements (*create_spectral_waves* and *simulate_dynamic_wave*).  Inside this compound, the input displacements are added together then applied to the input surface.\n\n- The final displaced result is then shaded basically and output.","library_dependencies":{"Amino":"2.15.0.9","bif":"2.15.0.9","fields":"2.15.0.9","ocean":"2.15.0.9","scatter":"2.15.0.9"},"graph_ports":[{"portName":"collider","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"ocean_surface","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"}],"terminal_states":[],"counts":{"nodes":38,"connections":53,"values":202,"compounds":4},"node_types":{"Core::Graph::pass":4,"Core::Math::multiply":4,"Simulation::Ocean::simulate_foam":2,"Core::Math::clamp":2,"Value::float":2,"assign_ocean_diagnostic":1,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_plane":1,"Simulation::Ocean::create_spectral_waves":1,"Simulation::Ocean::displace_by_wave":1,"Simulation::Ocean::wave_set_foam":1,"Dummy_Geo":1,"Simulation::Ocean::dynamic_wave_settings":1,"Simulation::Ocean::simulate_dynamic_wave":1,"Simulation::Ocean::source_dynamic_wave":1,"calculate_cusp_scale":1,"Geometry::Properties::set_geo_property":1,"Rendering::Materials::assign_material":1,"Rendering::Materials::standard_surface_mat":1,"Rendering::Materials::set_geo_property_reference":1,"Geometry::Properties::get_geo_property":1,"Core::Math::SRT_to_matrix":1,"Core::Conversion::scalar_to_vector3":1,"Core::Math::sin":1,"Core::Time::time":1,"Modeling::Points::transform_points":1,"Core::Math::cos":1,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_sphere":1,"Core::Math::absolute_value":1,"Core::Fields::fractal_noise_field":1},"edge_type_pairs":{" -> Rendering::Materials::standard_surface_mat":7,"Value::float -> Core::Math::multiply":3,"Simulation::Ocean::simulate_foam -> Simulation::Ocean::wave_set_foam":2,"Simulation::Ocean::create_spectral_waves -> Core::Graph::pass":2,"Core::Math::multiply -> Core::Conversion::scalar_to_vector3":2,"Simulation::Ocean::displace_by_wave -> assign_ocean_diagnostic":1,"Simulation::Ocean::wave_set_foam -> Simulation::Ocean::displace_by_wave":1,"Modeling::Primitive::create_mesh_plane -> Simulation::Ocean::wave_set_foam":1,"assign_ocean_diagnostic -> ":1,"Core::Graph::pass -> ":1,"Dummy_Geo -> Core::Graph::pass":1,"Core::Graph::pass -> Simulation::Ocean::displace_by_wave":1,"Simulation::Ocean::dynamic_wave_settings -> Simulation::Ocean::simulate_dynamic_