name":"fractal_noise_field.ratio","type":"float","value":"0.5f"},{"path":"root/calculate_cusp_scale","name":"fractal_noise_field.frequency_ratio","type":"float","value":"0.5f"},{"path":"root/calculate_cusp_scale","name":"fractal_noise_field.time_ratio","type":"float","value":"1.5f"}],"compounds":[{"path":"root","name":"Graphs::Ocean::dynamic_boat_wake","metadata":{"compoundIsGraph":"true","author":"Autodesk","category":"Ocean","description":"A procedural ocean surface with simulated wake and foam.","documentation":"dynamic_boat_wake_docs_${language}.md","_notes":[{"type":"sticky_note","text":"Animated dummy geo.  Feel free to replace with your own."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# Wave Generation\n\nIn this section, the wave, wake and wave obstructions are generated.\n\n***source_dynamic_wave***\nThis compound takes in a mesh and uses it to generate obstruction and height maps for use in the ocean system.\n\n***dynamic_wave_settings***\nHere are all the settings for the ***simulate_dynamic_waves*** compound.  These are the settings for any simulated waves - wakes, collisions etc.\n\n\n***create_spectral_waves***\nThe non-dynamic waves in the graph.  This will generate any waves and displacement that do not need to be simulated - the ocean surface etc."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# Foam Generation\nIn this section, the foam is setup and simulated using the data generated in the last section.\n\n***simulate foam***\nThis compound simulates a dynamic foam image to be used in displaying and rendering foam on an ocean object.\n\nIn this example, separate simulate foam compounds are used to get finer foam control on the boat wake (*simulate_dynamic_foam*) and the wave foam (*simulate_spectral_foam*).\n\n***wave_set_foam***\nThis takes the ocean surface object and samples foam positions based on that.  It will also set a foam property on the geometry."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# Ocean Displacement (and diagnostic)\n\nThe ***displace_by_wave*** is what brings all the ocean data together.  It adds up all the displacements and applies them to the provided mesh.  It takes in the *geometry*\n and displaces it with the *waves* inputs.\n\nIn this case, the *geometry* input has a *foam* property."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"Using a ***fractal_noise_field*** to generate the *cusp_scale*."}],"_backdrops":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Double-click for more information"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Generate Wave Displacements"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Generate Foam"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Displace and Shade"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Ocean Surface Mesh"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Simulated"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Procedural"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Double click for more info"}]},"ports":[{"portName":"collider","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"ocean_surface","portDirection":"output","portType":"Object"}],"terminal_states":[],"node_count":16,"connection_count":19,"value_count":134},{"path":"root/assign_ocean_diagnostic","name":"assign_ocean_diagnostic","metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/${language}/assign_diagnostic_material.md"},"ports":[{"portName":"geometry","portDirection":"input","portType":"Object"},{"portName":"base_color","portDirection":"input","portType":"Math::float3","metadata":[{"metaName":"UIWidget","metaType":"string","metaValue":"ColorPicker"}]},{"portName":"specular","portDirection":"input","portType":"float","metadata":[{"metaName":"UiSoftMin","metaType":"string","metaValue":"0"},{"metaName":"UiSoftMax","metaType":"string","metaValue":"1"}]},{"portName":"specular_roughness","portDirection":"input","portType":"float"},{"portName":"subsurface","portDirection":"input","portType":"float"},{"portName":"subsurface_scale","portDirection":"input","portType":"float"},{"portName":"transmission","portDirection":"input","portType":"float"},{"portName":"transmission_depth","portDirection":"input","portType":"float"},{"portName":"foam_color","portDirection":"input","portType":"Math::float3","metadata":[{"metaName":"UIWidget","metaType":"string","metaValue":"ColorPicker"}]},{"portName":"geometry_with_material","portDirection":"output"}],"terminal_states":[],"node_count":7,"connection_count":17,"value_count":50},{"path":"root/Dummy_Geo","name":"Dummy_Geo","metadata":{"_notes":[{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# Animated Geometry\n\nTo showcase the system, the geometry needs to move for best results.\n\nThis section uses cosine and sine operations to produce a basic animation with which we transform the dummy geo."}],"_backdrops":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Animation\n"}]},"ports":[{"portName":"geometry","portDirection":"output"}],"terminal_states":[],"node_count":12,"connection_count":14,"value_count":10},{"path":"root/calculate_cusp_scale","name":"calculate_cusp_scale","metadata":{"_notes":[{"type":"sticky_note","text":"Using a ***fractal_noise_field*** to generate values returns an output roughly between *-magnitude* and *magnitude*.  The values are made all positive with ***absolute_value*** and then ***clamp*** is used to set the range desired. "}],"_backdrops":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Genrate values"}]},"ports":[{"portName":"clamped","portDirection":"output"}],"terminal_states":[],"node_count":3,"connection_count":3,"value_count":8}],"teaching_notes":[{"type":"sticky_note","text":"Animated dummy geo.  Feel free to replace with your own."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# Wave Generation\n\nIn this section, the wave, wake and wave obstructions are generated.\n\n***source_dynamic_wave***\nThis compound takes in a mesh and uses it to generate obstruction and height maps for use in the ocean system.\n\n***dynamic_wave_settings***\nHere are all the settings for the ***simulate_dynamic_waves*** compound.  These are the settings for any simulated waves - wakes, collisions etc.\n\n\n***create_spectral_waves***\nThe non-dynamic waves in the graph.  This will generate any waves and displacement that do not need to be simulated - the ocean surface etc."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# Foam Generation\nIn this section, the foam is setup and simulated using the data generated in the last section.\n\n***simulate foam***\nThis compound simulates a dynamic foam image to be used in displaying and rendering foam on an ocean object.\n\nIn this example, separate simulate foam compounds are used to get finer foam control on the boat wake (*simulate_dynamic_foam*) and the wave foam (*simulate_spectral_foam*).\n\n***wave_set_foam***\nThis takes the ocean surface object and samples foam positions based on that.  It will also set a foam property on the geometry."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# Ocean Displacement (and diagnostic)\n\nThe ***displace_by_wave*** is what brings all the ocean data together.  It adds up all the displacements and applies them to the provided mesh.  It takes in the *geometry*\n and displaces it with the *waves* inputs.\n\nIn this case, the *geometry* input has a *foam* property."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"Using a ***fractal_noise_field*** to generate the *cusp_scale*."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"# Animated Geometry\n\nTo showcase the system, the geometry needs to move for best results.\n\nThis section uses cosine and sine operations to produce a basic animation with which we transform the dummy geo."},{"type":"sticky_note","text":"Using a ***fractal_noise_field*** to generate values returns an output roughly between *-magnitude* and *magnitude*.  The values are made all positive with ***absolute_value*** and then ***clamp*** is used to set the range desired. "}]}